   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 282 of the laws of 2008, relating to authorizing the town of East Hampton, county of Suffolk to issue certain serial bonds, in relation to permitting the issuance of such serial bonds to liquidate a deficit for the year 2009, increasing the aggregate principal amount for such serial bonds for 2007, 2008 and 2009; and extending the provisions thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S6730",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6730-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1, Chap 282 of 2008",
    "lawSection": "Suffolk County",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6730\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend chapter 282 of the laws of 2008, relating to\nauthorizing the town of East Hampton, county of Suffolk to issue\ncertain serial bonds, in relation to permitting the issuance of such\nserial bonds to liquidate a deficit for the year 2009, increasing the\naggregate principal amount for such serial bonds for 2007, 2008 and\n2009; and extending the provisions thereof\n\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis legislation would authorize and extend the provisions of the Town\nof East Hampton, County of Suffolk, to issue certain serial bonds.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 of Chapter 282 of the Laws of 2008, relating to authorizing\nthe Town of East Hampton, County of Suffolk to issue certain serial\nbonds, as amended by Chapter 190 of the Laws of 2009, is amended to\nauthorize the Town to issue serial bonds on or before December 31,\n2011, in an aggregate principal amount not to exceed $30,000,000 for\nthe specific purpose of liquidating actual general fund deficits for\nfiscal years ending December 31, 2007, December 31, 2008, and December\n31, 2010. It further provides that in anticipation of the issuance and\nsale of such serial bonds, bond anticipation notes are authorized to\nbe issued.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe Town of East Hampton has issued debt in the form of Bond\nAnticipation Notes in the amount of $15,000,000 pursuant to provisions\nestablished by Chapter 282 of the Laws of 2008 (extended by Chapter\n190 of the Laws of 2009). However, an audit conducted by the State\nComptroller's Office identified a number of problems with the Town's\n2009 budget which could present a significant shortfall, coupled with\nother emerging issues that could have a serious negative impact on the\nTown's general fund deficit. As a result, the Town of East Hampton is\ncurrently seeking to authorize an additional $15,000,000 in serial\nbonds. This legislation authorizes the Town to issue serial bonds on\nor before December 31, 2011 in an aggregate principal amount to not to\nexceed $30,000,000 for the specific object or purpose of liquidating\nactual deficits in its general fund at the close of the fiscal years\nendings December 31, 2007, December 31, 2008 and December 31, 2009.\nThis legislation is necessary to address the worse than anticipated\ncondition of the Town of East Hampton's finances and operating fund\ndeficits. In addition, the Town will be taking a number of significant\nactions to ensure the events of the last four years do not reoccur.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
